== Cook lentils ==

Place the @toor dal{1%cup} with @turmeric{½%tsp} and water in a #pot, #pressure cooker or #Instant Pot liner{}.

> See FAQs above for more on how to do this.

Cook the dal until very creamy. Use a #whisk to lightly beat the dal until it's creamy.

== Make the tempering or "tadka" ==

Heat the @oil{1%tbsp} in a wide #saucepan, #Dutch oven{} or #karahi, then add the @black mustard seeds{1%tsp} and @cumin seeds{1%tsp} and @?asafetida{¼%tsp}, if using.

> Use any oil of your choice, including avocado oil, sunflower oil, grapeseed oil, peanut oil or coconut oil.

As soon as the mustard seeds sputter, add the @cilantro{2%tbsp} and @?curry leaves{2%sprigs} and the @green chili peppers{1-2}(cut into thin strips, deseeded for less heat).

> Use green chili peppers like jalapeno or serrano.

Sauté the cilantro and curry leaves for ~{1%minute}, then stir in the @tomatoes{2%medium}(finely diced). Cook the tomatoes until they have expressed most of their juices and are very soft.

== Add the lentils ==

Add the cooked dal to the #saucepan and mix well. Add water to thin out the lentils - I add about a cup. Bring the dal to a boil, lower heat to simmer, cover and cook for ~{5%minutes}. This gives the flavors a chance to meld.

Turn off the heat, then add in the @lemon juice{½%lemon} and @salt{to taste} and garnish with more cilantro before serving.